        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Financial Accounting",
        "topic": "Depreciation Methods",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2021",
        "question_text": "<p>Under the <b>straight-line method</b> of depreciation, if an asset costs $10,000, has a residual value of $2,000, and a useful life of 4 years, what is the annual depreciation charge?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The straight-line depreciation formula is: <b>$(Cost - Residual Value) / Useful Life$</b>. Thus, ($10,000 - $2,000) / 4 = $2,000 per year.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
